7em}\\mathbf{i}-2xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}.$"] [17592186180093 "Which of the following vector fields have a stream function?\n\nI. $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=4xy\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+{y}^{4}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$\n\nII. $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=\\operatorname{cos}(3x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+3y\\operatorname{sin}(3x)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$\n\nIII. $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)={e}^{xy}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}-y{e}^{x}\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$"] [17592186180173 "![](images/0e/0e4a78829ce8d1135d46dda1db59c968c0306937d9c5a45b24fa41648a679ea4.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a line segment from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(2,0),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(2,0)$ to the point $B(1,1).$\n\nGiven that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=2,\n$$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(x+y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+(x-y)\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j},$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$"] [17592186180175 "![](images/51/512905447203d1d3a96781d20d586f9c4cf5cc9392fab50607b6fc77e9b00121.png)\n\nThe path ${C}_{1}$ consists of a section of the parabola $y={x}^{2}$ from the point $O(0,0)$ to the point $A(2,4),$ and the path ${C}_{2}$ consists of a line segment from the point $A(2,4)$ to the point $B(0,4).$\n\nGiven that $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=-2,\n$$ evaluate $$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r,\n$$ where $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=x\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{i}+y\\hspace{0.167em}\\mathbf{j}$ and $C={C}_{1}\\cup {C}_{2}.$"] [17592186180278 "Evaluate the integral $$\n\\displaystyle \\int_{C}\\sin \\left(\\frac{πy}{4}\\right)ds\n$$ along the line segment from $(1, 0, 1)$ to $(2, 2, 3)$."] [17592186198584 "Consider the vector field $\\mathbf{F}$ and the surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v),$ where\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{F}(x,y,z)=⟨xz,\\hspace{0.222em}2y,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩,\\hspace{1em}\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨uv,\\hspace{0.